src/mccvk.h -- provenance and license

src/mccvk.h declares the subset of the Vulkan ABI that src/mccgpu.h binds: the
~40 core entry points the width-ladder oracle calls, the handle and flag types
they take, and the structures those calls read and write. The declarations are
transcribed from the Khronos Vulkan-Headers project (vulkan/vulkan_core.h and
vulkan/vk_platform.h), which is distributed under the Apache License 2.0:

    https://github.com/KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Headers
    Copyright 2015-2025 The Khronos Group Inc.
    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

A copy of the Apache License 2.0 is at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Two mechanical differences from the upstream headers, both required by this
repository's host-gate invariant, which forbids raw platform macros outside
src/mcchost.{h,c}:

  - the stdcall attribute on Windows is selected with MCC_HOST_WIN32 rather than
    _WIN32;
  - the 64-bit non-dispatchable handle representation is selected by testing
    UINTPTR_MAX rather than the upstream architecture macro list. The two agree
    on every platform where both are defined; the upstream list is exactly the
    set of targets with 64-bit pointers.

The upstream armeabi-v7a "hardfloat" calling convention case is not reproduced;
mcc does not support 32-bit Android as a host.

Layout equivalence with the upstream headers was verified by compiling the same
sizeof/alignof/offsetof/constant census against both headers and diffing: 242
facts identical on x86_64 and on i386.
